7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Argument
function createArgument(argument, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the argument against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the learning record reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate an argument ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, date_created now, student_id from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the argument.

Step 7. Insert the premise records, the assumption records, the counterargument records, the response records, the fallacy records, and the assessment records.

Step 8. Insert the learning link and the work link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the argument_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Argument
function readArgument(argumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the premises, the assumptions, the counterarguments, the responses, the fallacies, the assessments, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Argument
function updateArgument(argumentId, argument, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new argument.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the argument_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Argument
function deleteArgument(argumentId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the argument_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Arguments
function queryArguments(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching arguments.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the arguments, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Arguments
function aggregateArguments(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching arguments.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the arguments and the count.

7.8 Export Argument
function exportArgument(argumentId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each argument, call createArgument.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching arguments.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per argument. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Argument
function moderateArgument(argumentId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the argument_id and the status.

7.12 Argument Graph
function argumentGraph(argumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Build the graph with the premises, the assumptions, the conclusion, the counterarguments, and the responses as nodes, and the support, attack, and defense relations as edges.

Step 4. Return the graph.

7.13 Argument Comparison View
function argumentComparisonView(conclusionStatement, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all arguments with the same conclusion.

Step 3. Build the comparison by overlaying the premises, the assumptions, the counterarguments, and the responses.

Step 4. Return the comparison.

7.14 Fallacy Map
function fallacyMap(argumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Build the map with the fallacies placed at their locations.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.15 Student Progress View
function studentProgressView(studentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all arguments for the student.

Step 3. Build the view with the argument strength, validity, and soundness over time.

Step 4. Return the view.

7.16 Find Related Arguments
function findRelatedArguments(argumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Find arguments with the same conclusion, the same subject, or the same argument type.

Step 4. Return the related arguments.

7.17 Audit Log
function auditLog(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Return the results.

7.18 Backup
function backup(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. If sql, dump as SQL. If json, dump as JSON.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the output and the format.

7.19 Restore
function restore(file, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Load the database from the file.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the status restored.

